meta {
  name: Node CPU/memory utilization
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseURL}}/recommendations/openshift/nodes
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  limit: 10
  offset: 0
  filter[term]: medium
  filter[engine]: cost
  ~filter[cluster]: 
  ~filter[node]: 
  ~filter[category]: idle
  ~filter[category]: overcommitted
  ~filter[category]: underutilized
}

headers {
  x-rh-identity: {{xRhIdentity}}
}

docs {
  Canonical path for node CPU and memory utilization recommendations (deprecated alias: `/nodes/utilization`).

  Filters: filter[term] (short|medium|long), filter[engine], filter[category],
  filter[instance_type], filter[machineset_name], filter[tag:<key>]=<value>.

  filter[category] is the unified classification filter replacing the former
  filter[is_underutilized], filter[is_overcommitted], filter[stranded_resource],
  and filter[idle_state] parameters.
  Valid node categories: idle, overcommitted, stranded_cpu, stranded_memory, underutilized, optimized.

  Nested response shape (per node):
  - classification: category (unified field)
  - metrics: cpu_util_p50, cpu_util_p95, mem_util_p50, mem_util_p95
  - recommendation_terms.medium_term.recommendation_engines.cost|performance:
      recommended_cpu_cores, recommended_memory_gib, node_count_reduction,
      estimated_monthly_savings (currency object with value/unit)

  Also: pod_capacity, pod_scheduling_headroom, machineset_name, suggested_instance_type,
  instance_type_reason.

  RBAC: requires cost-management.openshift.node (node name scope) and
  cost-management.openshift.cluster (cluster UUID scope). Users without matching
  permissions receive empty data[], not 403.

  Fleet consolidation groups by instance_type when present, else similar allocatable capacity.
  See "Node recommendations - consolidation" for node_count_reduction examples.

  Per-node recommendation history: N/A (no GET .../nodes/{node}/history). Use fleet
  GET .../history for container snapshots only. Quality metrics (GET .../quality) are
  container-scoped, not node-scoped.
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.meta.count: isNumber
  res.body.data: isArray
}
